    "Opposite caps of minimum leaves contain unique minimum leaves, defining a finite cycle. Distinct cycle opposite caps cannot nest (unique contained leaf) or cover F in a pair (wF>2m), so they are disjoint. Their removed corridors are nonempty and zero-edge.",
